---
import MarketingPage from '../layouts/MarketingPage.astro';

const description = 'Why I built Shiba: AI employees for the work behind a company, with human approval, reviewable results, and software you can self-host.';
const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: 'Why I Built Shiba: AI Employees for the Work Behind a Company',
  description,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Prince Pal', sameAs: ['https://github.com/princepal9120'] },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Shiba', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://tryshiba.dev/assets/mascot/shiba-logo-512.png' } },
  datePublished: '2026-09-26',
  dateModified: '2026-11-01',
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://tryshiba.dev/why-shiba/',
  image: 'https://tryshiba.dev/assets/og/shiba-og.png',
};
const examples = [
  ['Engineering', 'Fix a bug, add a test, and explain the change.'],
  ['Design', 'Draft a user flow, interface copy, or a design specification.'],
  ['Marketing', 'Turn product notes into a launch brief and editable campaign copy.'],
  ['Sales & revenue', 'Prepare an account brief, outreach draft, or summary of supplied pipeline notes.'],
  ['Operations', 'Write a release checklist, handoff, or recovery runbook.'],
  ['Finance', 'Organize supplied expense information or prepare a draft budget for human review.'],
];
---

<MarketingPage
  title="Why I Built Shiba — AI Employees for Company Work"
  description={description}
  path="/why-shiba/"
  type="article"
  publishedTime="2026-09-26T00:00:00Z"
  modifiedTime="2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"
  schema={articleSchema}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Why Shiba', path: '/why-shiba/' }]}
>
  <section class="shell hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">A note from the founder</p>
    <h1>More help with company work.<br /><em>The final say stays with you.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">Shiba is an AI employee workspace for the work behind a company: engineering, design, marketing, sales, operations, finance, and research. Describe the task, approve the proposed work, and review what comes back.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button" href="/docs/getting-started/">Start with one task <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a class="button button-outline" href="https://github.com/opentoolsorg/shiba" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="shell story">
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="origin-title">
      <p class="section-label">01 / Where it started</p>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="origin-title">I wanted more choice in how agents worked.</h2>
        <p>I started with coding agents. I used Devin alongside local tools and wanted to choose the model for each task, run the software in my own account, and inspect the result.</p>
        <blockquote>I wanted Devin-level background execution — with my own tools, my own routing, and a clear point where I could say yes or no.</blockquote>
        <p>That became Shiba. The aim is broader now: help with the work around a company, from a code change to the brief, research, and operating notes that go with it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="section-work">
      <p class="section-label">02 / The work</p>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="section-work">Start with a useful piece of work.</h2>
        <p>An employee is a working brief: what to do, what context to use, and what to hand back. These are examples of responsibilities you can give one.</p>
        <dl class="work-list">
          {examples.map(([role, task]) => <div><dt>{role}</dt><dd>{task}</dd></div>)}
        </dl>
        <p>The built-in starting templates are Engineering, Marketing, Research, and Operations. Use custom instructions for other roles. A role does not connect your accounts or give permission to publish, send messages, update a CRM, or move money.</p>
        <p>For now, every execution needs a GitHub repository, including document work. It provides context and a place for the files. You review the actual output before using it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="section-ask">
      <p class="section-label">03 / Your decision</p>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="section-ask">Keep the important decisions visible.</h2>
        <ul class="principles">
          <li><strong>Choose the scope.</strong> Give a concrete task and say what a useful result looks like.</li>
          <li><strong>Approve the request.</strong> Read the repository, task, and publishing choices before standard repository execution starts.</li>
          <li><strong>Review the result.</strong> Inspect the files, changes, and reported checks. A finished task still needs your judgment.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The conversation stays in a thread, so you can discuss the result without starting the context again. Another execution still follows its approval flow.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="section-devin">
      <p class="section-label">04 / Choosing a tool</p>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="section-devin">Factual comparison: Devin Cloud vs. Shiba</h2>
        <p>Devin helped shape the original question, but Shiba is not a claim of feature parity or a benchmark result. Choose the tool that fits the work and the responsibility your team wants to take on.</p>
        <p>Shiba's source is available under <strong>AGPL-3.0-only</strong>, and you can run it in your own Cloudflare account. The software is free to self-host; hosting and model usage cost extra. You also take responsibility for setup, access, and operation.</p>
        <p>Try a small task you can check, then judge the output, the review effort, and the actual cost. The <a href="/open-source-devin-alternative/">evaluation guide</a> gives you a starting checklist.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing-section" aria-labelledby="section-deploy">
      <h2 id="section-deploy">Try one task before changing your workflow.</h2>
      <p>Shiba is still under development. Start with a low-risk task and review <a href="/docs/readiness/">deployment readiness</a> before using it for live work.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" href="/docs/getting-started/">Read the quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="button button-outline" href="/waitlist/">Follow the project</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</MarketingPage>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 104px); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .hero h1 { max-width: 1000px; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); }
  .hero .lead { max-width: 68ch; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .hero-actions .button { min-height: 44px; }
  .story-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(120px, .7fr) minmax(0, 3fr); gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 80px); padding-block: clamp(44px, 7vw, 80px); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .section-label { margin: 8px 0 0; font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .prose-body { min-width: 0; max-width: 850px; }
  .prose-body h2, .closing-section h2 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.2vw, 2.8rem); text-wrap: balance; }
  .prose-body p, .closing-section p { max-width: 68ch; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.75; }
  .prose-body blockquote { margin: 28px 0; padding-left: 22px; border-left: 2px solid var(--navy); color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .work-list { margin-block: 28px; }
  .work-list > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; padding-block: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .work-list dt { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .work-list dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.65; }
  .principles { padding-left: 1.2rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .principles li { margin-block: 16px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .principles strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .closing-section { max-width: 760px; padding-block: clamp(44px, 7vw, 80px); }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .story-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 18px; } }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .work-list > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; } .hero-actions .button { width: 100%; } }
</style>
